{number: 75}
{title: Nearer, My God, to Thee}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[F] Nearer, my [Bb] God, to [F] Thee,
[Bb] Nearer to [C7] Thee!
[F] E'en though it [Bb] be a [F] cross
That [C7] raiseth [F] me;
Still all my [Bb] song shall be,
[F] Nearer, my God, to Thee,
Nearer, my [Bb] God, to [F] Thee,
[Bb] Nearer [C7] to [F] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[F] Though like the [Bb] wander-[F] er,
The [Bb] sun gone [C7] down,
[F] Darkness be [Bb] over [F] me,
My [C7] rest a [F] stone;
Yet in my [Bb] dreams I'd be
[F] Nearer, my God, to Thee,
Nearer, my [Bb] God, to [F] Thee,
[Bb] Nearer [C7] to [F] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[F] There let the [Bb] way ap-[F] pear
Steps [Bb] unto [C7] heav'n;
[F] All that Thou [Bb] sendest [F] me
In [C7] mercy [F] giv'n:
Angels to [Bb] beckon me
[F] Nearer, my God, to Thee,
Nearer, my [Bb] God, to [F] Thee,
[Bb] Nearer [C7] to [F] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[F] Then, with my [Bb] waking [F] thoughts
Bright [Bb] with Thy [C7] praise,
[F] Out of my [Bb] stony [F] griefs,
Bethel [C7] I'll [F] raise;
So by my [Bb] woes to be
[F] Nearer, my God, to Thee,
Nearer, my [Bb] God, to [F] Thee,
[Bb] Nearer [C7] to [F] Thee.
{end_of_verse}
